$ render-plate --version
exit 0
0.1.0

$ render-plate --help
exit 0
render-plate — render motion/slide plates from plates.json, each alone, to renders/plates/<id>.mp4

Usage: render-plate [options] <plates.json> (<plate-id>... | --all)

For each plate: plates/<id>/index.html is kept if it exists (hand-authored) or written from the
template for its kind (templates/motion, templates/slide); brand/ (the brand pack) and
vendor/gsap.min.js are refreshed; the composition is rendered on its own at the plates.json
fps and size; the MP4 must last durationMs ±1 frame. Live plates are refused (use video-capture).
Project folders (plates/, renders/plates/, review/) live next to plates.json unless --out is given.

Options:
      --all              Every motion and slide plate in plates.json (live plates are skipped)
      --brand <pack>     Brand pack folder or brand.json (overrides plates.json "brand")
      --out <dir>        Project folder for plates/, renders/plates/ and review/ (default: the plates.json folder)
      --sheet            Also write review/contact-<id>.jpg (a frame every --every)
      --every <time>     Contact-sheet interval with --sheet, e.g. 0.5s or 250ms (default: 0.5s)
      --lint             Run hyperframes lint and check --strict on each plate before rendering; any failure stops
      --storyboard       Do not render: snapshot one key frame per plate into review/storyboard.jpg (stage 4)
      --scaffold-only    Only prepare plates/<id>/ (template, brand, GSAP); do not render
      --rescaffold       Overwrite an existing plates/<id>/index.html from the template
      --quality <level>  HyperFrames render quality: draft, looks, standard, high or delivery (default: standard)
      --json             Print the results as JSON
  -h, --help             Show this help and exit
      --version          Print the plugin version and exit

Examples:
  render-plate plates.json --all --sheet
  render-plate plates.json p2-table --lint
  render-plate plates.json --all --storyboard
  render-plate docs/build/fixtures/F1/plates.json --all --brand brand-packs/default --out /tmp/f1

